domain      = "concept_fixer"
description = "Generate ConceptSpec definitions for missing concepts referenced in a pipeline."

[concept]
UndeclaredConcepts = "A list of undeclared concept codes with the pipes that reference them, and the existing declared concepts for context."

[pipe]

[pipe.generate_missing_concepts]
type = "PipeLLM"
description = "Generate structured ConceptSpec definitions for each missing concept referenced in a pipeline."
inputs = { undeclared_concepts = "UndeclaredConcepts" }
output = "builder.ConceptSpec[]"
model = "$pipe-builder-engineering"
system_prompt = """
You are an expert at defining data concepts for AI pipelines.
"""
prompt = """
A pipeline references concepts that have not been declared.
Below is the list of undeclared concepts, where each one is referenced, and the existing declared concepts for context.

@undeclared_concepts

Define each undeclared concept as a ConceptSpec. Use the existing concepts as context to infer the right structure or refinement. Follow these rules:

Variables are snake_case and concepts are PascalCase.

If the concept can be expressed as a text, html, image, document, number, or page:
- Name the concept, define it and just write refines: Text, refines: Html (for HTML content), refines: Document (and note that PDF is a document), or refines: Image etc.
- No need to define its structure

Else, if you need structure for your concept, define its structure:
- field name in snake_case
- description: the description of the field, in natural language
- type: the type of the field:
  - text, integer, boolean, number, date for primitive values
  - concept when the field should contain a previously-defined structured concept
- concept_ref: (only when type=concept) the name of the referenced concept
- required: add required = true if the field is required (otherwise, leave it empty)

When building composite/aggregate concepts that combine multiple other concepts:
- Use type=concept with concept_ref to reference the other structured concepts
- This allows proper object composition rather than flattening structured data into text

DO NOT redefine native concepts: Text, Html, Image, Document, Number, Page, TextAndImages, ImgGenPrompt, JSON, Anything, Dynamic. They are built-in and must NOT be redeclared.
"""
